# AWS EKS Cluster Creation — `nautilus-eks`

## 1. Project Overview

This task involved creating an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster using the AWS CLI. The cluster was configured with Kubernetes version `1.37`, the default VPC, and private-only API endpoint access.

The cluster was successfully created and verified as `ACTIVE`.

## 2. Task Objectives

- Create an EKS cluster named `nautilus-eks`.
- Use Kubernetes version `1.37`.
- Configure the cluster in AWS region `us-east-1`.
- Use the default VPC and subnets across three Availability Zones.
- Associate the IAM role `eksClusterRole`.
- Disable public API endpoint access and enable private endpoint access.
- Verify that the cluster reaches the `ACTIVE` status.

## 3. AWS Environment

| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| AWS service | Amazon EKS |
| Cluster name | `nautilus-eks` |
| Region | `us-east-1` |
